---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Example from '../components/Example.astro';
import CodeViewer from '../components/CodeViewer.astro';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<DocsLayout title="Get started" active="guide">
<p class="doc-kicker">START HERE</p><h1>Get started</h1><p class="prose">Copy the stylesheets from the repository’s dist folder into your project. No consumer build step or browser JavaScript is required. This is an alpha preview; npm publication remains on hold.</p>
<Example id="installation" title="Load the stylesheet" description="Native HTML receives defaults automatically. The optional font stylesheet loads bundled Manrope; keep its fonts directory next to it." render={false} html={'<!doctype html>\n<html lang="en" data-theme="auto">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="utf-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">\n  <title>My RevaCSS page</title>\n  <link rel="stylesheet" href="reva-fonts.css">\n  <link rel="stylesheet" href="reva.css">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class="container">\n    <h1>My first page</h1>\n    <button type="button">Save changes</button>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>'}/>
<Example id="native" title="Start with native HTML" description="No button class is needed. Labels and input types remain ordinary HTML." html={'<label for="start-email">Email</label>\n<input id="start-email" type="email" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com">\n<button type="button">Save changes</button>'}/>
<Example id="page-settings" title="Configure once on html" description="All core settings can supply page-wide defaults. Tables, controls, images and supported layouts inherit them without repeating attributes." render={false} html={'<html data-theme="dark" data-accent="violet"\n      data-table="striped" data-size="large"\n      data-width="narrow" data-gap="large">'}/>
<p>Omit settings to keep the defaults. Override only what differs: a local <code>data-table="plain"</code> removes stripes; <code>data-size="medium"</code> resets control size; <code>data-ratio="auto"</code> restores natural image ratios. <a href={base+'attributes/#page-defaults'}>See a complete demo</a>.</p>
<Example id="local" title="Apply settings locally" description="The section supplies inherited settings. A nearer attribute can override them." html={'<section data-accent="violet" data-shape="subtle" data-density="compact">\n  <article class="card">\n    <h3>Your project</h3>\n    <p>Local settings apply to supported descendants.</p>\n    <button type="button">Violet action</button>\n    <button type="button" data-accent="teal">Teal override</button>\n  </article>\n</section>'}/>
<Example id="scoped" title="Style part of an existing page" description="Use the scoped stylesheet and configure the .reva boundary or its descendants. Each boundary starts with its own defaults. It is a CSS scope, not Shadow DOM isolation. Overlay markup must remain inside the boundary." render={false} html={'<link rel="stylesheet" href="reva.scoped.css">\n<section class="reva">\n  <button type="button">A scoped control</button>\n</section>'}/>
<h2>Choose what to explore</h2><p><a href={base+'components/buttons/'}>Buttons</a>, <a href={base+'components/forms/'}>forms</a>, <a href={base+'components/layouts/'}>cards and layouts</a>, <a href={base+'components/top-menu/'}>top menu</a>, <a href={base+'attributes/'}>shared data attributes</a> and <a href={base+'themes/glass/'}>glass material</a> each include demos and HTML.</p>
<h2>Customise with ordinary CSS</h2><CodeViewer id="custom-css" lang="css" label="Custom CSS" code={':root {\n  --re-primary: #7041cf;\n  --re-primary-end: #5228a4;\n  --re-on-primary: #fff;\n}\n.product { padding: 2rem; }'}/><p>Override both gradient stops and verify contrast. <a href={base+'reference/'}>See the public tokens</a>.</p>
<h2>Supply meaningful HTML</h2><p class="prose">Provide labels, descriptive links, alternative text and explanatory errors. CSS supplies appearance; it does not invent error messages or announce application updates. Native interactions remain subject to their documented behavior.</p>
<p class="prose">Manual keyboard, screen reader, text spacing, zoom and real device checks remain release requirements.</p>
</DocsLayout>
